<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 6 June, from 1523 to 1984.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1523</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gustav Vasa is elected King of Sweden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Strängnäs the Swedish estates chose Gustav Eriksson Vasa, leader of the revolt against Danish rule, as king. He broke with Rome and laid the foundations of the Swedish state. The day is now Sweden's National Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1844</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Williams founds the YMCA in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A draper's assistant, George Williams, and eleven friends founded the Young Men's Christian Association to support young workers in the city. It spread worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1918</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Marines attack at Belleau Wood</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American Marines launched costly assaults on German positions west of Château-Thierry. Three weeks of fighting helped halt the German drive on Paris.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1933</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First drive-in cinema opens in New Jersey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard Hollingshead opened his 'Automobile Movie Theatre' at Pennsauken, near Camden. Drive-ins became a fixture of post-war American suburban life.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1944</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied armies land in Normandy on D-Day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">About 156,000 Allied troops landed by sea and air on the Normandy coast. The invasion opened the long-awaited second front against Germany in Western Europe.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1984</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexey Pajitnov completes the first version of Tetris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Working at a Soviet Academy of Sciences computing centre in Moscow, Pajitnov finished his falling-block puzzle game. It became one of the best-selling video games in history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></li></ol>
